course: dictionary
lesson: 10534
title: Ugly: more than looks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ugly most often means not nice to look at. «The old shed was ugly, with broken windows and peeling paint.» But the same word can describe other things, so you have to read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «The argument turned ugly when the players started shouting.» Nothing here is about looks. Turned ugly means the situation became nasty. Ask yourself: is the sentence about how something looks, or how something feels and behaves?
explain: «An ugly cut» and «ugly storm clouds» are about danger, not plainness. Clues like cut and storm tell you the meaning. Try swapping in not nice to look at: if it doesn't fit, look for another meaning.
explain: Calling a person ugly is hurtful. «A face for radio» is a joking, unkind way to say someone is ugly, and it still hurts. So think about how a word makes people feel, as well as what it means.
fact: Ugly means not nice to look at.
fact: «Ugly» can also describe something nasty or unpleasant, like «an ugly fight» or «an ugly mood».
fact: «Ugly» can describe something that looks dangerous, like «an ugly cut».
fact: «Turn ugly» means a situation became nasty.
fact: In «The Ugly Duckling», looks can change and do not show who someone really is.
exercise: «The argument turned ugly when the players started shouting.» What does turned ugly mean? | Pretty and bright | It stopped raining | *It became nasty and unpleasant | It got very quiet
exercise: «The Eiffel Tower was called ugly when it was new.» What does ugly mean here? | Very kind | Made of stone | *Not nice to look at | Very tall
exercise: Why is calling someone «ugly» hurtful? | *Because it is unkind and makes people feel bad | Because it means they are very tall | Because it is a long word | Because it means they are clever
test: «He had an ugly cut on his knee.» What does ugly suggest here? | *Something that looks dangerous | Something very funny | Something very cheap | Something very old
test: What does «The Ugly Duckling» teach? | Ducks should always stay in ponds | *Looks can change and do not show who someone really is | Ugly things must be hidden | Yellow ducks are the best
exam: «He was in an ugly mood after losing the match.» What does ugly mean here? | Very tired | Happy and loud | Not nice to look at | *Nasty and unpleasant
